[0.442, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.037, "o", "Run, inspect and fix each monolith worktree's services (Dev Control Center).\r\n\r\nUsage: dev-center [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  gui        Open the app, or bring it forward on this worktree's Services page\r\n  status     Live state of every service: PID, port, URL, CPU, memory, errors\r\n  context    A Markdown brief of this worktree for an LLM: status, wiring, recent failures and the\r\n             exact commands to fix things. No secrets\r\n  urls       Every service's stable URL in this worktree\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  worktrees  The monolith worktrees the app knows, with what each is running\r\n  tabs       Active worktree tabs in activation order. Needs the running app\r\n  setup      Show or change Setup: the main monolith (new worktrees come from it), the dump folder\r\n             and the PostgreSQL/Redis tools (saved in the repository's local git config), and\r\n             whether shared downloads are kept (a per-user setting)\r\n  doctor     Check the app, URL router, database tools, manifest and required programs\r\n  sign-in    Sign the running app in to Crafting or 1Password, as its Sign in button does (`cs\r\n             login` in the browser, or 1Password's approval), and wait up to 5 minutes for the\r\n             result. A service identity (SANDBOX_CONFIG_DIR, OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN) is only\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "             checked again, never an interactive sign-in; so is an app without a window\r\n  logs       A service's recent output (plain text unless --raw)\r\n  start      Start services, consoles or profiles (dependencies start too)\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  stop       Stop services (Ctrl-C, then SIGTERM, then SIGKILL to that service only)\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  restart    Stop and start services again\r\n"]
