[0.008, "o", "For LLMs and other callers:\r\n1. Run `dev-center version` first. Do not assume commands or JSON fields from\r\n   another version exist in this one.\r\n2. Read `dev-center help <command>` before using a command's flags.\r\n3. Start every investigation with `dev-center context` (or `status --json`).\r\n   It tells you what is running, what failed, recent failure output, how the\r\n   services are wired and the exact commands for this worktree.\r\n4. Read-only commands are always safe: `help`, `manual`, `version`,\r\n   `status`, `context`, `urls`, `worktrees`, `tabs`, `logs`, `doctor`, `database`\r\n   (no options), `database --shared`, `setup`, `display` and `editors` (no\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "   options), `main` (fetches, changes nothing), `create --dry-run`,\r\n   `open --dry-run`.\r\n"]
